; SOURCE\T001.BPC, table 1's module: code and data the main program loads
; anywhere and relocates by adding its base to every dword T001.REL lists
; (docs/bpc-module.md), unpacked from the archive in ILLUSION.EXE by
; tools/illfiles.py. The list says exactly where the offsets are
; (doskit's `offrel`); the header's resource slots carry flags in their
; top two bits. Nothing is entered at 0: the main program calls the
; module through the header's pointers.
bin        build/files/SOURCE/T001.BPC noentry
offrel     build/files/SOURCE/T001.REL flags=C0000000
segment    CODE 0 CODE             ; the whole file, code and data

name       CODE:0000 HEADER        ; 45 dword slots, copied relocated to the main program's CODE:F3E4 (docs/bpc-module.md)
words      CODE:0080 1 CODE        ; slot 32
words      CODE:009C 3 CODE        ; slots 39..41
code       CODE:37AD MOD_BALL_BONUS ; slot 32: the end-of-ball bonus (docs/bpc-module.md): the audio record to host +04h; the player's bonus shown over eight rounds of "BONUS" (every other round the multiplier's text record, by the player's word +12h n/2 - 1), the combos (a word per player at 5750h, each 1,000,000 in the total; "n COMBO(S)"), then "TOTAL BONUS" and the total (the number ending at state+2AC8h) or "NO BONUS"; in C in port/src/modcode.c, one routine for the four tables (docs/HANDOFF.md, "GAME_PHASE 5 in the port"); run 2026-09-30 with a poked bonus, multiplier and combos: equal to the port's
code       CODE:00B4 MOD_LOADED    ; slot 39: called once the module is loaded and its resources resolved (main program CODE:B287); a RET
code       CODE:00B5 MOD_GAME_START ; slot 40: called at a game's start (main program CODE:2AA6D); a RET in table 1
code       CODE:00B6 MOD_NEXT_BALL ; slot 41: called at the next player's ball (main program CODE:2BD61)
comment    CODE:00B6 with the current player's record (state+0D76h) word +12h n not 0 (the bonus multiplier, presumably): slot-16 counter 4502h (thresholds 1..6) set to n/2 in its words +6 and +16h for the current player (state+0D72h), and the first n/2 light states of the chain at 942Eh (next +10h, lights 2..6) get the player's bit (state+0D74h) in byte +5, so the counter's lamps come back for the player's ball. An odd n would not end the loop at 2 steps (not checked whether it occurs)
comment    CODE:00A8 slot 42: 0, and relocated (in T001.REL): the module's base once loaded

; 16-bit addresses without a register (67h, the main program's cells at
; DS:0..3Fh) are written DS:[SMALL n]. A DS prefix where DS is the default
; (3E), EBP the index, as in ILLUSION.386; its displacement an offset, so
; the line is DB, DD label, DB
raw        CODE:394C

; the opcode-14h object of mode stream 5EA8h (command 5EE0h), table 1's
; shooting game on the display (docs/bpc-module.md, "Table 1's shooting
; game"): two methods the main program calls (CODE:2DBAD, CODE:2CFC8)
name       CODE:9A46 SHOOT_OBJECT
words      CODE:9A46 2 CODE
code       CODE:9A4E SHOOT_START   ; the object's +0: hits 0, lives 4, window 1, score 0, the windows' delays
code       CODE:9B25 SHOOT_UPDATE  ; the object's +4, once a frame: the street, the windows, the flippers, the crosshair
name       CODE:9E2D SHOOT_WINDOWS ; the four windows of the state from +12h: timers, steps, looks, the hits and the bad guys' shots
name       CODE:A0F9 SHOOT_PIC     ; picture ECX+1 of the table at FS:0 to the display at ES:[PIC_OFFSET], PIC_WIDTH x PIC_HEIGHT, rows 160 apart, 0FCh added to each byte; ES and FS from host vector +28h
name       CODE:A142 SHOOT_PIC_TRANSP ; as SHOOT_PIC, bytes 0 left out (transparent)
name       CODE:A193 PIC_WIDTH
name       CODE:A197 PIC_HEIGHT
name       CODE:A19B PIC_OFFSET
name       CODE:A19F SHOOT_STATE   ; hits, lives, the crosshair's window, the flippers' repeats, the 25-hit flag, the score, the four windows (docs/bpc-module.md)
